Regression test: slide sorter accessibles disposed while a call waits for the SolarMutex.

AT-SPI clients reach the gtk3 accessibility bridge from the main loop, which runs with the
SolarMutex released; another thread holding it (a UNO client terminating the office) can dispose
the slide sorter's accessibles and destroy the slide sorter meanwhile. HST Draw crashed on Linux
(SIGSEGV in SlideSorterModel::GetPageDescriptor from AccessibleSlideSorterObject::getAccessibleName
or getAccessibleStateSet) when the AT-SPI tree had been walked and the office was terminated over
UNO. The test holds the SolarMutex, starts the call on another thread, disposes the accessible slide
sorter view and expects DisposedException.

License: the new test file is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the makefile keeps MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y.
